            <div xml:id="d444">

                <pb facs="0661" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1946v06/pg647"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">871.00/11–346: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative in Rumania</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Berry</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-11-03T10:00:00+02:00">November 3, 1946—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 4—4:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1027. Groza in expansive mood recently told of secret meeting with Tito.<anchor
                        n="35" xml:id="d444-f1"/> Tito assured him as long as Moscow was satisfied
                    with Rumanian Govt he had nothing to ask from Rumania adding if there were Govt
                    in Rumania with which Moscow was not satisfied he would revise his attitude.
                    Groza cited this conversation as evidence that happy future of Rumania was
                    closely tied to continuation of his Govt. In same conversation he said his Govt
                    planned to strengthen the church in Rumania as it was weapon that would be used
                    against the imperialism of Vatican. In this connection he is drafting law
                    arranging for retirement of some independent-thinking bishops in Transylvania
                    and replacement by men more in sympathy with new DPM order.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Berry</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d444-f1" n="35" xml:id="d444-f1-content">
                <p>Josip Broz-Tito, Yugoslav Prime Minister.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
